<!--
  jewel-ranger.xml — golden fixture (DESIGN §7.4 case: JEWEL / RADIUS / CONVERSION).

  Intent: a level-1 Ranger whose passive tree allocates the path out to a Jewel
  Socket node (tree node 60735), with a Diamond jewel base present in the item
  library. This anchors the jewel/radius mechanism: a jewel socket is the tree
  anchor whose radius a socketed jewel would affect, and allocating it exercises
  the jewel-socket node handling in the tree + calc path. The allocated node set
  below is the exact connected path the upstream core produced via
  PassiveSpec:AllocNode out to that socket, so it loads deterministically.

  NOTE (humanGate=gamedata, honest limitation): the vendored PoB2 core's
  ItemsTab:Load binds a tree-socketed jewel by its PoB item URL (SocketIdURL
  pbURL), not by a local item id, so a jewel cannot be round-tripped into a tree
  socket purely from a self-contained, asset-free XML in this version. This
  fixture therefore anchors the jewel-SOCKET (radius anchor) allocation path
  deterministically and keeps the Diamond jewel in the library as the documented
  jewel base, rather than fabricating an unsupported binding (NO-FALLBACK).

  Provenance (humanGate=gamedata): authored from upstream save formats
  (TreeTab:Save + ItemsTab:Save). NO live scraping, NO bundled GGG assets.
  gamedata IDs used:
    - class: Ranger  (PoB2 spec classId/classInternalId = 2)
    - tree version: 0_5
    - jewel socket node: 60735  (isJewelSocket)
    - allocated passive path: 1140, 13828, 15507, 21280, 28050, 35901, 48401,
      50459, 60735, 61312, 63888
    - item base: Diamond  (Bases/jewel.lua, type "Jewel")
-->
